00:07:23.039 --> 00:07:29.599 align:start position:19%
&gt;&gt; Good evening everyone. My name is Joseph
Lucero. I'm a senior at Srian East High

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:34.240 align:start position:19%
School and I've had the opportunity to
serve as heads chair on Mayor's Youth

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:37.360 align:start position:19%
Council this evening uh this year.
Tonight, I want to talk a little bit

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:42.400 align:start position:19%
about my experience in Mayor's Youth
Council in our capstone project. I had

00:07:40.479 --> 00:07:46.319 align:start position:19%
no idea what Mayor's Youth Council was
to start the year. I almost wasn't even

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:51.280 align:start position:19%
in it. I missed the application
deadline, but luckily Brooks, who knew

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:56.800 align:start position:19%
my parents, reached out and said I'd be
a great candidate. So, I got an

00:07:53.599 --> 00:08:00.879 align:start position:19%
interview and I got accepted. And I'm
really glad that happened because it's

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:04.400 align:start position:19%
probably been one of the most impactful
experiences I've had throughout my high

00:08:02.479 --> 00:08:07.440 align:start position:19%
school career. And one of the coolest
parts was the people. Through Mayor's

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:10.960 align:start position:19%
Youth Council, I met students from
different schools and different parts of

00:08:09.039 --> 00:08:14.560 align:start position:19%
the community that I probably would not
have met otherwise. People from schools

00:08:12.879 --> 00:08:19.120 align:start position:19%
I normally would not interact with
became some of my friends. And it wasn't

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:23.120 align:start position:19%
just meetings either. There was always
something going on before, after, or in

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:26.319 align:start position:19%
between. I do not think there was a
meeting where people didn't say

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:31.840 align:start position:19%
afterwards and talk about school life
events or what's happening around town,

00:08:28.639 --> 00:08:34.959 align:start position:19%
the drama at other high schools.
It turned into more than just a

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:38.640 align:start position:19%
leadership group. It was like a
community. And I think that says a lot

00:08:37.039 --> 00:08:42.640 align:start position:19%
because bringing students together from
different backgrounds in schools is not

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:46.480 align:start position:19%
always easy, but somehow it worked.
Another thing that stood out to me was

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:49.920 align:start position:19%
how personal the experience felt. The
mayor was not just someone who showed up

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:53.920 align:start position:19%
for official events and disappeared
afterwards. He took time to talk to us

00:08:51.839 --> 00:08:58.160 align:start position:19%
and get to know us, and he was genuinely
a part of our group. One of my favorite

00:08:56.240 --> 00:09:01.519 align:start position:19%
memories was our Christmas party. It was
a fun event and it was one of those

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.440 align:start position:19%
nights you remember because everybody
was hanging out, talking, doing the gift

00:09:03.519 --> 00:09:08.880 align:start position:19%
exchange, sharing cookies, and having
fun. And the mayor was there with us. He

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:12.959 align:start position:19%
wasn't there in a formal role. He wasn't
giving speeches. He was just a part of

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:16.800 align:start position:19%
it. And little things like that made the
experience feel really real. He would

00:09:14.959 --> 00:09:20.560 align:start position:19%
always keep us updated on his Dualingo
streak and how Spanish learning was

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:23.680 align:start position:19%
going, which I always thought was pretty
funny and made him feel really

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:27.279 align:start position:19%
relatable.
Then there was our capstone project. We

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:31.519 align:start position:19%
wanted to do something that would
directly help people in our community.

00:09:29.519 --> 00:09:34.959 align:start position:19%
So, we created care packages for people
experiencing homelessness. We put

00:09:33.279 --> 00:09:39.279 align:start position:19%
together backpacks filled with thermal
base layers, toiletries, hand sanitizer,

00:09:37.519 --> 00:09:43.040 align:start position:19%
wipes, toothbrushes, and other
essentials. We ended up making 50

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:46.480 align:start position:19%
backpacks for men and another 50 for
women. Originally, we planned on working

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:50.399 align:start position:19%
with another organization, but things
changed and we had to adjust. We ended

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:54.240 align:start position:19%
up partnering with the Welcome Mat, and
I honestly think that made the project

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:57.920 align:start position:19%
even better. We got to meet them, hear
about the work they do, and it gave us a

00:09:56.240 --> 00:10:02.800 align:start position:19%
better understanding of the needs in our
community. About a week after putting

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:06.720 align:start position:19%
everything together, we dropped off the
backpacks and got to see the idea become

00:10:04.959 --> 00:10:09.680 align:start position:19%
something real. And I think that project
represents what May's Youth Council is

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:13.680 align:start position:19%
about. It's not just learning about
issues, it's also about doing something

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:16.880 align:start position:19%
about them. This year changed the way I
looked at leadership. It showed me that

00:10:15.279 --> 00:10:20.959 align:start position:19%
leadership is not always standing in
front of people. Sometimes it's

00:10:18.079 --> 00:10:24.720 align:start position:19%
listening. Sometimes it's serving.
Sometimes it's working alongside people

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:29.600 align:start position:19%
and helping where you can. And it showed
me that students can make a real

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:34.320 align:start position:19%
difference. I want to thank the mayor,
the adviserss, Devon, Brooks Cotton, and

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:38.079 align:start position:19%
everyone who helped with our project.
And all the students in May's Youth

00:10:35.839 --> 00:10:41.760 align:start position:19%
Council. Thank you for the friendships,
the memories, the opportunities, and

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:46.600 align:start position:19%
everything this experience brought. I'm
really grateful I got to be a part of

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:46.600 align:start position:19%
it. Thank you.

00:10:52.959 --> 00:10:59.360 align:start position:19%
Thank you, Joseph. Mayor Collins, if you
